  "limitations": [
    "Models both sides of Whitehall, including the open Tiltyard and Horse Guard Yard, the Cockpit, Tennis Court, service ranges, and the linked palace and river lodgings. Inaccessible interiors, precise room divisions and unrecorded secondary structures are outside this exterior reconstruction.",
    "The surveyed plans constrain the surviving hall, major courts and the enclosure. The Cockpit roof, lost facades, heights, glazing and roof profiles are interpretive.",
    "The date selects a representative 1670 snapshot with local shoreline and grade edits. The 2.21 m Thames stage is a visualization. The surrounding London map and other structures follow the host’s data."
  ],
